A||N||3||Haze_Performance||Eibach Spring Help?||||4||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||09-02-2000||11:09 PM||||So I heard that if you put Eibach's on your car it's possible for the spring's to become unperched under high speed turning or driving over an uneven road. How do I keep them seated? Mostly I'm having problem's with the driver's side rear. <P><BR>Thanks<BR>Carl <P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg">   <B>1985 Sport Coupe </B><P><BR><B>Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A></B>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Oreif||09-03-2000||12:02 AM||||Haze, I drilled some holes and used nylon tie wraps to hold the springs in place. You need to do this top and bottom. One on each side is sufficent to hold them. (Total of 4 2 top and 2 bottom) Generally I did it so when the car is jacked up they don't unseat. I drove for 2 months without the tie wraps and never unseated them. What are you doing to unseat them? High speed U-turns on RailRoad tracks? Jumping over ricers?<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||09-03-2000||12:13 AM||||It happens over bumps of all sizes. I hear a load thud in the drivers side rear. I took it to the exhaust shop and checked it out. When it was in the air the spring is seated but alittle loose.||||reg||7
Z||000003||maninblack||09-03-2000||12:43 AM||||Haze:I use the same spring an dhave no problem with it so far,may be you should get the guys who install it to recheck it for you.otherwise it could be the wrong application.||||reg||1
